# Generate Commit Message (sparkles)

Cursor Source Control sparkles only reads this file (not `.cursor/rules` or AGENTS.md).

When generating a Git commit message for this repository:

1. Output exactly **1–2 lines** in English. No bullets, no file lists, no "Made-with: Cursor".
2. Format:

```text
<type>: <short topic>

<one purpose-oriented sentence>
```

3. `<type>` must be one of: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `refactor`, `test`, `chore`, `perf`, `ci`
4. Subject: brief area/topic only (not a changelog). Body: one sentence on **why** / purpose.

Good:

```text
feat: map loading UI

Show basemap as soon as MapLibre loads so travel-layer delays do not block the map.
```

Bad (do not generate this style):

```text
Refactor OutbreakMap loading logic and improve error handling

- Enhanced the loading process by implementing a timeout...
- Improved error handling for map loading events...
```
